{{/*
Alertmanager has no UI of its own here: --web.external-url points at Grafana's
alert page, and there is no ingress to the Service (see alertmanager-service.yaml).

The default email template builds its "View in AlertManager" button as
  {{ .ExternalURL }}/#/alerts?receiver={{ .Receiver | urlquery }}
and Grafana renders that hash suffix as an EMPTY rule list ("You haven't created
any rules yet"), while the same URL without it lists every rule. Overriding this
one template - the only thing in the default email that uses it - sends the
button to the working page. Found on jwilleke/mjs-ha#117.

Per-alert "Source" links are separate: they come from the rule engine
(Prometheus, or Loki's ruler.external_url + datasource_uid) and are not affected.
*/}}
{{ define "__alertmanagerURL" }}https://grafana.nerdsbythehour.com/alerting/list/{{ end }}
